2 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "11"} "1936 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "12"} "1948 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "14"} "1956 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "15"} "1960 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "16"} "1964 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "17"} "1968 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "18"} "1972 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "19"} "1976 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "20"} "1980 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "21"} "1984 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "22"} "1988 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "23"} "1992 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "24"} "1996 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "25"} "2000 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "26"} "2004 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "53"} "2008 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "65"} "2010 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "54"} "2012 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "67"} "2014 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "59"} "2016 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "69"} "2018 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "61"} "2020 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "63"} "2024 Summer Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/ATH'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Athletics at the 1952 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "20 – 27 July 1952"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "33"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/368"} "Helsingin Olympiastadion, Helsinki"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "The world had not recovered somewhat from the ravages of World War II, and the level of athletics competition was increasing yearly. The 1952 Olympics saw the début of athletes from the Soviet Union, who had competed at the 1946 and 1950 European Championships, but had passed on the " [:a {:href "/editions/12"} "1948 Olympics"] ", for rather Byzantine reasons. Germany also competed again, after they were not invited in 1948. Titularly Germany was to be represented by a combined team from East and West Germany, but the German team was entirely from West Germany, as the East Germans refused to compete alongside their Western counterparts."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The 1952 Olympics were opened by two Finnish track legends. The torch was brought into the stadium at the Opening Ceremony by " [:a {:href "/athletes/67728"} "Paavo Nurmi"] ", the greatest athletic star in the Finnish pantheon. He then handed it to " [:a {:href "/athletes/67641"} "Hannes Kolehmainen"] ", winner of the " [:a {:href "/results/56634"} "5K"] " and " [:a {:href "/results/56642"} "10K in 1912"] " and the " [:a {:href "/results/57135"} "marathon in 1920"] ", who lit the Olympic Flame. Having been opened by distance runners, it was fitting that the Helsinki Olympics were the private party of the great Czechoslovakian runner " [:a {:href "/athletes/76736"} "Emil Zátopek"] ". Zátopek won the 5,000/10,000 double in dominating fashion. He had never before run a " [:a {:href "/results/58937"} "marathon"] ", but elected to enter that race as well, and won quite easily, completing a unique Olympic distance triple. His family did quite well, as his wife, " [:a {:href "/athletes/76547"} "Dana Zátopková"] ", won the " [:a {:href "/results/59232"} "women’s javelin"] " gold medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The German team won no events, but collected two silvers and three bronze medals. The Soviet men did not win any gold medals, but " [:a {:href "/athletes/77336"} "Galina Zybina"] " won the " [:a {:href "/results/59214"} "shot put"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/77292"} "Nina Romashkova-Ponomaryova"] " the " [:a {:href "/results/59223"} "discus throw"] "."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table ta